From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:06:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: look for firmware-N.bin without the
 user-space fallback

ath11k_fw_pre_init() asks for firmware-2.bin through
ath11k_core_firmware_request(), that is firmware_request_nowarn(), and
falls back to API 1 when the file is not there. The file is optional,
and many installations have none.

With CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK enabled,
firmware_request_nowarn() can still hand a missing file to the user-space
loader. This makes every probe wait for a uevent and its response before
ath11k can fall back to API 1.

Request the optional API-N firmware with request_firmware_direct()
instead. This checks the filesystem only and does not invoke the
user-space fallback loader.

Based on the upstream patch:
https://lore.kernel.org/ath11k/20261101-b123-fw-api-n-direct-v1-1-a9b734520abc@gmail.com/

Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
index ef1b4c81843a3..3628e33e57f6e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
@@ -16,10 +16,14 @@ static int ath11k_fw_request_firmware_api_n(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	struct ath11k_fw_ie *hdr;
 	const u8 *data;
 	__le32 *timestamp;
-
-	ab->fw.fw = ath11k_core_firmware_request(ab, name);
-	if (IS_ERR(ab->fw.fw)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(ab->fw.fw);
+	char path[100];
+
+	/* The file is optional: look for it on the filesystem only, so a
+	 * missing one does not go through the user-space fallback loader.
+	 */
+	ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, name, path, sizeof(path));
+	ret = request_firmware_direct(&ab->fw.fw, path, ab->dev);
+	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "failed to load %s: %d\n", name, ret);
 		ab->fw.fw = NULL;
 		return ret;
-- 
